WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.690
Gai! You've got to hang on!

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:07.860
Big Brother Gai!

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:17.580
The cyborg, Gai Shishioh, has been pushed to his physical limit...

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.700
...in the endless battle with the Zonders.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.870
Hell and Heaven!

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.460
Hell and Heaven is a double-edged sword.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.590
Controlling such massive amounts of energy has taken a grave toll...

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.880
...on the cyborg's body.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:01:00.790
There's no choice but to continue the fight even as it grinds away his soul.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:05.750
Could that simply be the cruel fate bestowed upon heroes?

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.160
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.060
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:19.970
King of Braves GaoGaiGar

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:24.060
Rise in fury, Steel Cyborg!

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:30.780
With your red mane and golden arms!

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.060
Your G-Stone sparkling in the sun...

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.980
All the world's hope is in your hands.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:43.900
Your time has come to make a stand!

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.700
Crushing the hopes of the people...

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.460
The Zonders will pay the price!

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.460
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.630
Ga-Ga-Ga, Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.170
Final Fusion, approved!

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:04.300
Now transform into a superhero!

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.260
Warping dimensional space!

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:11.340
Dividing Driver!

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.980
A miracle! A mystery! The truth! A dream!

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:24.860
A gigantic, invincible guardian is born!

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:27.810
Our very own King of Braves!

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.700
Ga-Ga-Ga-Ga, GaoGaiGar!!

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.750
This is the story of the brave men and women...

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.710
...who fight with all their hearts to save mankind.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:39.130
Midday Demon

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.220
<i>Midday Demon</i>

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.600
Hey guys, it's lunchtime! Time for fun!

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:52.060
All righty, let's start today's edition of "Laugh 'Til You Drop! Midday..."

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.360
Shut up!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.650
For crying out loud! Every last one of you!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.240
Tokyo University

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.070
Why do you have to keep disrupting my studies?

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.660
Nothing but Tokyo University!

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.570
TOKYO U. or bust!

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.830
Examinees have to keep working whether it's night or day!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.790
For gosh sake, how many years do you think I've been plugging away?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.630
Darnit, darnit, darnit, darnit!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.510
Isn't there anything that'll give me some relief?

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.180
All that pent-up stress inside... It would be better to let it out.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.190
What the...

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.730
If you're going to relieve your stress, you must do it with pizzazz!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:38.190
For the sake of your health, and for your soul, as well.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.410
Hope you'll consider joining!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.620
This way for all aspiring manga editors!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.350
I don't believe this.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.810
This is the 5th straight day...

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:14.310
It's been going after top universities in Tokyo, as well as top prep schools.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:19.230
And every target was hit at the same time everyday, 12:01 PM!

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.150
All at the same time, too?

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.320
Entohji, what about the results of your probe?

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.120
The satellite search didn't pick up any Zonder-like traces...

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:30.240
...or any traces of Elementary Particle Z0, for that matter.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.540
Just as I thought, they're all the same.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.460
All right, you're fine. Now stop.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.380
Okay, hold on tight now!

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.380
Man, I can't believe how huge this crater is...

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.890
It's almost like a meteor crashed, or something.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:49.890
Meteor?

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.730
Yeah, sure! No way!

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:58.400
Actually, this meteor idea might not be as far off base as you think.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.650
Well, how's that?

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.150
Take a look at the screen.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:05.280
This crater wasn't made just by an explosive impact.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.530
It looks like a depression created by the fall of some colossal object.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.910
A colossal object?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.830
Hey, tell me what happened here!

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.330
I heard a really loud sound...

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.630
What kind of sound?

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:22.670
It was after the explosion, I heard a sound like a gust of wind...

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.800
After the explosion?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.590
Just as I thought...

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.760
The noise came after the sound of the impact.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:31.640
In other words, proof that something moving faster than...

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.850
...the speed of sound hit the ground!

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:37.230
Entohji, we're going to need you to recalculate everything...

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.480
...from infall velocity to angle of incidence!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.610
Right.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.740
We've got our results now.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.240
The area was bombarded by a gigantic cannon.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.240
A cannon?

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:52.450
There's no mistake, all the data bears out my theory.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.250
In that case, we must take immediate action!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.870
The thing is...

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.750
Even the giant warship Yamato from the last century...

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.920
...only had a 46cm caliber cannon.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:06.340
My rough calculations indicate that this cannon's at least 80cm.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.010
Oh, great!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.970
Hold up! That just can't be right.

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:14.600
There's no such thing as an 80cm-caliber cannon...

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:15.560
No, Major...

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:17.690
Actually, there is just one...

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.980
The largest cannon known to man, the 80cm caliber railway gun built...

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.820
...by the Wehrmacht... the Gustav Gun!

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:37.250
Zonder!

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:48.800
But what would a railway gun built by the Germans be doing in Japan?

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:53.510
The second Gustav gun has been missing since the end of World War II.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.310
But recent discoveries show that it was secretly...

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.440
...transported to Japan just before the war ended.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:02.810
Not only that, but it's been modified to fit the Japanese rail system!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.860
Are you saying that a colossal weapon...

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.030
...from over 60 years ago has been resurrected?

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.780
And if it's been Zonderized, which would give it a massive power boost...

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.530
The shell's velocity would be 3 to 4 times the speed of sound.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.830
A head-on attack would be more or less impossible!

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.750
Zonder!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:21.870
Then what options do we have?

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.920
If we can't attack head-on, dissipating the explosion itself should work.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.550
You mean use the Eraser Head!

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.340
What time is it now?

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.880
10:21.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:35.680
That gives us 1 hour and 40 minutes until 12:01.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:40.640
To estimate the impact point of a shell passing through the stratosphere...

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:45.860
...we'll use the Space Development Corporation's satellite tracking radar.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.700
Send out the GGG Freight Unit towards Hongou. Immediately!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.570
Hongou... did you say?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:55.950
Judging from the damage that's already been wreaked...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.790
...the enemy's next target is sure to be Japan's top university...

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:00.870
...Tokyo University!

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.210
Ballet Recital

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.590
I wonder when Hana's coming onstage?

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.010
Isn't that her right here?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.430
She was talking about dancing to the Doobie Brothers or something...

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.060
Excuse me, Ushi, but don't you mean DEBUSSY?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.690
Whatever! Who the heck cares, anyway?

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.400
Ah, ballet...

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:30.110
I started taking ballet lessons when I was two...

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:33.400
...but I quit because I didn't want my gorgeous legs to get all thick...

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.420
What should I do? I can't stop my heart from pounding...

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:49.880
Wait! The teacher said we should just pretend everybody's a potato...

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:53.050
They're all potatoes, they're all potatoes...

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.010
They're all...

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.720
...potatoes...

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:03.140
Oh, boy! They don't look like potatoes at all!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.810
It's 12 o'clock...

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.520
Picking up something on the satellite radar!

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.570
It's on a parabolic orbit!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.070
No mistake. It's an 80cm caliber cannon!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:16.660
What's the target?

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.530
Argh! There's so much to factor into my calculations!

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.910
Let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.580
All right, what do you say?

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.170
You were right on the money!
It's headed for Tokyo University!

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.130
HyoRyu! EnRyu! Prepare to launch at once!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.630
We've been waiting for your command!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:31.960
All right, let's do it!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.100
I'm not afraid, I'm not afraid, I'm not afraid...

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.680
System Change!

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.500
Symmetrical Docking!

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:26.980
ChoRyuJin!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:38.150
Just one second to succeed!

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.950
20 seconds until impact!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:52.540
Precision Firing Mode! Eraser Head Level 99!

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.940
We've succeeded!

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:19.990
The Eraser Head has dissipated 99.997% of the impact energy!

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.110
Good!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:27.540
A second round has just been fired!

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.910
Oh, my God!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.000
Only 48 seconds until impact!

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:32.120
What on earth...

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.130
No way!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:38.050
Normally, it'd take a Gustav Gun at least 10 minutes to fire another round!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:42.550
Its reloading capabilities have been boosted because it's been Zonderized!

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.180
I only have one option now...

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.150
Is he going to use himself as a shield?

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.720
I did it!

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.270
I managed to dance in front of everybody!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.270
You were awesome, Hana!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.230
What's going on?

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:38.650
ChoRyuJin!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.040
Target detected.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.830
You've got to hang on! HyoRyu! EnRyu!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.750
Don't worry, this is nothing.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.130
It'll take a lot more than that to bring us down!

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.680
HyoRyu will be undergoing repairs for at least 69 hours...

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.680
nice

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.100
Likewise, EnRyu will require approximately 82 hours...

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:54.730
At least they're both safe...

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:59.690
Apparently they were saved by undocking at the moment of impact.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.120
Still, they're both at Damage Level 5.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.490
There's no question that they were subjected to immense trauma.

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:16.410
What's going on?

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.040
I'm receiving an alert from Volfogg.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.710
He says he's discovered the Zonder's hideout.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.090
Good work, Volfogg.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.430
Please take a look at this.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.060
These are the coordinates of all the targets...

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.060
...and the estimated trajectory of the shell.

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:39.100
Normally, a railway gun is incapable of firing to the left or right.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:43.730
It is more or less restricted to firing along its own railway tracks.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.780
I see, so if we just reverse-calculate...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.320
That is correct.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.410
Is that the Zonder railway gun?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.740
Just look at the size of it!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:58.750
It's on the railway lines near Harinasan in Gunma Prefecture.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:02.130
They were abandoned before being completed in the last century.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.210
But what do we do now?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.340
We're up against a monster with a firing range of more than 80km!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.010
That thing can just pick us off before we get anywhere near it!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:10.840
No...

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.890
I have an idea.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:16.970
Gai!

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.890
Are you sure you should be up already?

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:23.810
HyoRyu and EnRyu put their lives on the line to protect everybody.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.230
I can't be lounging around in bed!

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:30.950
What in the world...

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:39.370
That's some loud tunneling they're doing over there...

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.380
Now that was a great big crow...

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:52.300
Now, Grandpa, you know that was a B-29!

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:56.310
Next stop, Takasaki, Takasaki...

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.060
That's an amazing pet!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.400
Are all the machines in sync?

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.820
Moving along according to plan.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:17.080
They're on course to join up on schedule at 11:59.

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.540
I never thought we'd attempt Final Fusion in front of the enemy.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:24.250
But getting too close will mean a direct hit from that 80cm-caliber shell.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.130
Not even GaoGaiGar could...

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.250
But he can't attack head-on if he stays too far back.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.880
The only option is to approach separately...

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.970
...without letting the enemy catch on.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:34.840
Current time, 11:45. The enemy should be emerging from that tunnel about...

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.640
...now.

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:40.060
We're counting on you, Gai!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.390
This is one move that we can't put off!

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:52.240
Zonder!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.120
All right! Start the operation!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.000
Fusion!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.430
GaiGar!

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:19.640
Final Fusion, approved!

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:24.020
Final Fusion!

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.230
GaoGaiGar!

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:18.160
How do you like that? You can't shoot behind you!

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.670
So the rails were part of that Zonder's body, too?

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:32.500
This isn't good!

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:38.470
Zonder!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.390
GaoGaiGar is unable to separate!

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:46.980
The energy emanating from the Zonder railway gun is increasing!

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.230
Make a run for it, Gai!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.730
Gai!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.230
I'm just gonna have to do it!

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.990
Chief! Launch the Dividing Driver!

00:18:59.110 --> 00:18:59.780
What did you say?

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:04.660
It's no good! It's way too close, we can't lock down the coordinates!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.160
Never mind that, just launch it!

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.540
Dividing Driver, launch!

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:32.310
Dividing Driver!

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:42.780
It actually warped space on the vertical!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:50.040
Oh! It's only a little at a time, but the energy from the cannon is decreasing!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:54.040
By bending space, he's trying make that mere 10 meter range count...

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:57.630
...for the cannon's entire maximum range of several hundred meters.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.350
Here comes the second shot!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.310
Gai!

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.560
I can't just give up over something like this.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.650
Or else how can I ever face HyoRyu and EnRyu?

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.240
It's no good!

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.650
It's not strong enough to bend back the energy of the blast!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:28.290
If I have to, I'll take your damage, and pay you back with interest!

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.500
You're gonna pay for what you did to HyoRyu and EnRyu!

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.250
At the end of the day, victory is OURS!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.420
Broken Magnum!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:56.190
The shell in the cannon is detonating! It's going to create a huge explosion!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.900
Gai, you've got to get that Zonder core right now!

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:01.570
Gai...

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.650
What's the matter, Gai?

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.120
Gai!

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:17.540
The Zonder has been silenced.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.630
Elementary Particle Z0, extinguished.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.720
GaoGaiGar is all right.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.680
Gai is alive!

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.400
Big Volfogg!

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.730
So you protected the Zonder core for me?

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.240
Yes. Special Agent Mamoru is here also.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.570
All right, then I'm leaving the rest to you...

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.450
Curatio!

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.290
Teneritas, sectio...

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:58.210
...salus, coctura!

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:08.340
Thank you!

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:11.930
From now on, I'm going to study at my own pace!

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.640
Retrieve all the Brave Robots at once!

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:25.740
Big Brother Gai!

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:28.570
Mamoru, why are you crying?

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:30.700
The battle's over now.

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:33.950
I know, but...

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:36.370
But...

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.420
I'm so glad...

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:50.310
You come floating down onto my planet.

00:22:51.510 --> 00:22:55.180
That's the dream I always have.

00:22:56.580 --> 00:23:01.360
Now you're looking up at the sky again...

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:06.150
and you're searching for me.

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:10.320
Longing to see you and be with you...

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:17.250
I know I feel it just as strongly as you.

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:24.010
Give us the wings to fly

00:23:24.010 --> 00:23:28.670
and set off into the galaxy.

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:34.010
When you and I are grown up...

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:40.910
someday in the Sea of Stars.

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:49.030
Now releasing the latest intelligence.

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:53.530
The moment he launches the Dividing Driver and Hell and Heaven...

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:56.660
...Osaka will become GaoGaiGar's final resting place.

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:59.790
It's up to the ultra-secret tools, the Dimensional Pliers...

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:02.750
...to repair that warped space!

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:05.460
Next episode of GaoGaiGar, King of Braves...

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:07.460
"Conqueror of Space"

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:06.670
Conqueror of Space

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:10.380
Make sure you stay tuned for the order..."Final Fusion Approved!"

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:15.220
Pliers

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:14.590
This is the Key to Victory!
